"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T05:28:20-07:00","id":236360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=236036#post236036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That's....my favorite scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026congrats\u2026? <br /> <br /> That doesn't change the fact that, if one is going to recommend the book, one should acknowledge that that scene occurs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T05:40:53-07:00","id":236385,"title":"","content":"Eh. I find that an excessive worry, and one that paints the book (or even just the scene) in a negative light without necessity.<br /> It's a book. A good book. Read it. Tell me what you think after you've read it. Things are simpler that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T08:20:44-07:00","id":236520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game#post235466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because of his origins, Bhagwei might be the one person with the most solid claim to inheriting the Scarlet Throne in the whole Dynasty, but he just doesn't give a shit and pretends to be a simple Ragara.</div> </div> </div> </div>A minor note but the Throne doesn't get inherited this way. There's no succession procedure within the law, and neither House Ragara nor House Cynis would sponsor his claim anyhow; both actively want to keep him the hell <i>away</i> from rulership. His main strength isn't his secret lineage but his mastery of the Heptagram and its graduates. He has a large web of sorcerers that owe him great debts, access to Bronze Faction allies, all manner of arcane lore and ancient artifice, and treaties with spirit courts. What Bhagwei means to do with all that should worry everybody with an eye on the Throne.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=235643#post235643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, well, Ragara is definitely the Empress' firstborn son, he is called out as being such in more than one source. Cynis was a woman and the major lines of the house descend from her, so it is likely she was a daughter rather than a consort of the Empress even if their union was facilitated with sorcery. Tepet and Cathak I'm not sure about.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's right on page 32 (Exalted: the Dragonblooded) that Manosque is born 9 years before Ragara; on page 26 Ragara spends his childhood &quot;with the ministers of the Thousand Scales rather than in the exercise yards or debaucheries favored by his older siblings&quot;. Ragara is not firstborn, though I'm curious if you remember where you saw mention of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=235903#post235903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I put Cathak, Peleps and Iselsi as being in what seems to be the same boat of Jerah; Houses that predate the children of the Empress, formed from the remnants of Shogunate families that pledged loyalty to her in the aftermath of the Contagion.</div> </div> </div> </div>We did something similar with Tepet, Peleps and Iselsi for our games; all were Shogunate families, with children of the Empress married in to both Peleps and Iselsi to bind them to the Throne. Tepet himself she took as her personal lover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T08:25:57-07:00","id":236526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=236034#post236034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is really tempting me to get Aspect Book: Wood. I can't remember if I'm already expecting it because of my kickstarted backing, though-...</div> </div> </div> </div>You can look forward to a confirmation that cells exist in Exalted, and that living things are made of them, as usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T08:36:43-07:00","id":236539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=236520#post236520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A minor note but the Throne doesn't get inherited this way. There's no succession procedure within the law, and neither House Ragara nor House Cynis would sponsor his claim anyhow; both actively want to keep him the hell <i>away</i> from rulership. His main strength isn't his secret lineage but his mastery of the Heptagram and its graduates. He has a large web of sorcerers that owe him great debts, access to Bronze Faction allies, all manner of arcane lore and ancient artifice, and treaties with spirit courts. What Bhagwei means to do with all that should worry everybody with an eye on the Throne.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not <i>quite </i>accurate.<br /> <br /> The thing about there being no succession procedure within the law is that people don't <i>default</i> to &quot;may the strongest win.&quot; Instead, people across the Realm are finding numerous ways to justify whoever they would like to see on the Throne, whether their criteria are strength of armies, religious devotion, administrative competency or just plain likeableness. In that context, even if succession isn't hereditary, the sense of legacy and familial momentum around an individual does matter in the eyes of people looking for the right candidate to support. The son of Ragara and Cynis would be someone outside the normal conventions of the Scarlet Dynasty, someone who bears the legacy of two Houses and as such, is beyond any single family's loyalty. There is something in that around which people could rally, a sense of being above these feuds. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T10:41:29-07:00","id":236658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=236520#post236520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's right on page 32 (Exalted: the Dragonblooded) that Manosque is born 9 years before Ragara; on page 26 Ragara spends his childhood &quot;with the ministers of the Thousand Scales rather than in the exercise yards or debaucheries favored by his older siblings&quot;. Ragara is not firstborn, though I'm curious if you remember where you saw mention of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manosque gets cut out of the official histories because of his family's rebellion. If there are any siblings between him and Ragara, I imagine that they mostly get forgotten due to lack of remarkable achievements, as is usual for the children of the Empress. I think the setting writing occasionally relies on the sort of historical abstraction I imagine they use in the setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T11:04:59-07:00","id":236698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=236034#post236034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is really tempting me to get Aspect Book: Wood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can recommend Aspect Book: Wood as well. As an Exalted player that started in 2e, it was still a great fluff read, but I didn't use the mechanics in the back. The fluff is worth the price of admission.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T20:58:57-07:00","id":237694,"title":"","content":"But can he tell you why kids love cinnamon toast crunch?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T15:19:50-07:00","id":238585,"title":"","content":"I actually have a soft spot for the Slug more than Ragara Bhagwei.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T18:01:49-07:00","id":238725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=235500#post235500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>My brother is a deeply compassionate being with an undying love for all life and life in and of itself. He is considerate, sensitive, patient and wise. For this reason, Ragara Bhagwei should never rule the Realm.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Because the narrator fears Bhagwei would dismantle the Realm's empire out of humanitarian concern?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T18:21:01-07:00","id":238732,"title":"","content":"I think compassionate, undying love for all life, considerate, and sensitive are being used to mean he's a totally pussy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T19:00:06-07:00","id":238762,"title":"","content":"I get a gist he's too smart to control and would be like Her Redness as a result: Implacable and pretty much in charge of the reigns top-to-bottom. It's the same reason folks seem to despise the very thought of Mnemon becoming Empress.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 08-24-2014, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T08:33:10-07:00","id":239165,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Awesome Elder Dynasts, who can forget Cathak Cainan? From what I recall, he is said to have such strong support from the Immaculate Order, the Legions and the general populace, that if he was at in interested in having the Scarlet Throne, the Great Houses would just immediately hand it over to him without a fight (unless I'm conflating him with Amber's Benedict again)! Are there any cool stories about him from Aspectbook: Fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T12:07:26-07:00","id":239393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=238725#post238725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Because the narrator fears Bhagwei would dismantle the Realm's empire out of humanitarian concern?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the implication is that being nice and caring about treating people fairly will probably make you last three weekends with hundreds of murderous, ambitious dragonblooded nobles gunning for your seat, unless you become markedly less worried about others' lives quickly. <br /> <br /> There's a general belief, which the narrator here clearly shares, that excessive worry for the wellbeing of your fellow man is a problem when trying to control a state that doesn't much want to be controlled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T12:22:39-07:00","id":239420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=239165#post239165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Awesome Elder Dynasts, who can forget Cathak Cainan? From what I recall, he is said to have such strong support from the Immaculate Order, the Legions and the general populace, that if he was at in interested in having the Scarlet Throne, the Great Houses would just immediately hand it over to him without a fight (unless I'm conflating him with Amber's Benedict again)! Are there any cool stories about him from Aspectbook: Fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall something mentioning that his support is lacking because, despite his awesomeness, he is getting old and showing none of Her Redness or Mnemon's unnatural longevity and people don't want to have to deal with another succession crisis anytime soon.*<br /> <br /> *Of course, this is ignoring the fact that it shouldn't have been that hard for someone to get him that 5 dot immortality hearthstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T16:56:13-07:00","id":239672,"title":"","content":"Basically if you're a major player, and you're backing a candidate, it's because you think you can keep them under your thumb after they're on the throne. That's why Mnemon has almost no backers among the major players; nobody thinks she'd be controllable. All her backers are people who think she has a chance to win and would rather end up the lackeys who backed the winner from the start.<br /> <br /> Nobody thinks Ragara Bhagwei could be kept under control, either, so he has no major player backers. And he hasn't really got any minor backers, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T17:01:52-07:00","id":239677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=239672#post239672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody thinks Ragara Bhagwei could be kept under control, either, so he has no major player backers. And he hasn't really got any minor backers, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>He at least <i>believes </i>that, were he to make a power play, he would have the influence that comes from having been the master of hundreds of sorcerers across the Realm, with the respect, favors and debts that come with it. The book doesn't really say if he is right in believing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T17:57:04-07:00","id":239734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=239672#post239672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically if you're a major player, and you're backing a candidate, it's because you think you can keep them under your thumb after they're on the throne. That's why Mnemon has almost no backers among the major players; nobody thinks she'd be controllable. All her backers are people who think she has a chance to win and would rather end up the lackeys who backed the winner from the start.<br /> <br /> Nobody thinks Ragara Bhagwei could be kept under control, either, so he has no major player backers. And he hasn't really got any minor backers, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. It's not his niceness his relative is worried about. It's his competence and general independence.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T18:20:50-07:00","id":239766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=236034#post236034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread is really tempting me to get Aspect Book: Wood. I can't remember if I'm already expecting it because of my kickstarted backing, though-...</div> </div> </div> </div>The DB Aspect books were not one of the benefits you could get from the Core KS. They'll likely be available as part of the DB KS though and probably at a price break.<br /> <br /> That said, AB: Water isn't particularly worth buying, so buying the other four Aspect Books will probably end up being about the same as the KS charges for all five, so I wouldn't worry too much about just buying AB: Wood now.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T20:51:06-07:00","id":239869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=239420#post239420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I recall something mentioning that his support is lacking because, despite his awesomeness, he is getting old and showing none of Her Redness or Mnemon's unnatural longevity and people don't want to have to deal with another succession crisis anytime soon.*<br /> <br /> *Of course, this is ignoring the fact that it shouldn't have been that hard for someone to get him that 5 dot immortality hearthstone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Huh, reading Mnemon's SoE write-up, she has a Stone of Immortality. Is this original to that book? ISTR reading that her unusual youth/lifespan was due to sorcerous experiments, trying to duplicate her mother's agelessness (also never explained, but most likely due to being attuned to the RDG). <br /> <br /> And yeah, I can think of a few ways the Bronze Faction can extend Cainan's life, if they really wanted to, so they should be able to. But I guess one could also come up with reasons those wouldn't work, to preserve the setting...He should go out in a literal blaze of glory, hoping to unite the Houses against their common enemy the Anathema by his example.<br /> <br /> If there's any DB in Creation who should go out with As In The Beginning, it's him!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T21:02:10-07:00","id":239889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=239869#post239869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Huh, reading Mnemon's SoE write-up, she has a Stone of Immortality. Is this original to that book? ISTR reading that her unusual youth/lifespan was due to sorcerous experiments, trying to duplicate her mother's agelessness (also never explained, but most likely due to being attuned to the RDG).<br /> <br /> And yeah, I can think of a few ways the Bronze Faction can extend Cainan's life, if they really wanted to, so they should be able to. But I guess one could also come up with reasons those wouldn't work, to preserve the setting...He should go out in a literal blaze of glory, hoping to unite the Houses against their common enemy the Anathema by his example.<br /> <br /> If there's any DB in Creation who should go out with As In The Beginning, it's him!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wanna say that AB: Earth claimed she stopped aging after the Versino exploded, but that might just be a faulty memory. There was also an Earth charm which would let you extend your lifespan indefinitely, provided you had good luck with the dice. <br /> <br /> And Sids can extend anyone's life indefinitely, because they have access to the Peaches of Immortality. I'm reasonably sure that Chejop could requisition one of them to ensure the stability of the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T21:37:01-07:00","id":239902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=239734#post239734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. It's not his niceness his relative is worried about. It's his competence and general independence.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>His competence is one thing, but there are plenty of brilliant Dragonblooded. It's how he would use the power of the Throne. That scene with the Ragaran satrapies highlights exactly what a hypothetical Emperor Bhagwei would do: begin unraveling the Thousand Mazy Paths in an effort to make the Realm more efficient and effective. When combined with his natural empathy and compassion, he would be putting House Ragara AND House Cynis out of business in short order. His dual heritage does him no favors in the race for the throne.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=239420#post239420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I recall something mentioning that his support is lacking because, despite his awesomeness, he is getting old and showing none of Her Redness or Mnemon's unnatural longevity and people don't want to have to deal with another succession crisis anytime soon.*<br /> <br /> *Of course, this is ignoring the fact that it shouldn't have been that hard for someone to get him that 5 dot immortality hearthstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The stuff about Cainan being too old isn't a general Realm support thing but specifically Chejop Kejak ruminating on whether to devote his considerable influence to pushing Cainan's candidacy. Cainan does have a great deal of respect from both the Immaculate Order and many soldiers within the Legions, plus the command of an entire Great House and possible alliances with the Ledaals and the V'neefs.<br /> <br /> The immortality hearthstone has to be treated as a non-factor, for reasons we'll get to below...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=239869#post239869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yeah, I can think of a few ways the Bronze Faction can extend Cainan's life, if they really wanted to, so they should be able to. But I guess one could also come up with reasons those wouldn't work, to preserve the setting...He should go out in a literal blaze of glory, hoping to unite the Houses against their common enemy the Anathema by his example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, the Bronze <i>can't</i> get Peaches of Immortality or Hearthstones of Immortality for Cathak Cainan or otherwise Kejak's worries about promoting him as a candidate would vanish entirely. Remember, Kejak does not see a worthy successor within House Cathak other than Cainan, and frets that he would be giving the Realm a brief few years of stability before crashing into a second calamitous civil war when Cainan surely dies. One can assume that Cainan is nearing the end of an already extended lifespan already from imperial anagathics (he's roughly 400 years old, after all), and that the Bronze granting their favorite prospect eternal life is off the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1564,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","user":"Shinjo","date":". 08-25-2014, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T22:00:09-07:00","id":239912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=239902#post239902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nah, the Bronze <i>can't</i> get Peaches of Immortality or Hearthstones of Immortality for Cathak Cainan or otherwise Kejak's worries about promoting him as a candidate would vanish entirely. Remember, Kejak does not see a worthy successor within House Cathak other than Cainan, and frets that he would be giving the Realm a brief few years of stability before crashing into a second calamitous civil war when Cainan surely dies. One can assume that Cainan is nearing the end of an already extended lifespan already from imperial anagathics (he's roughly 400 years old, after all), and that the Bronze granting their favorite prospect eternal life is off the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Other than to preserve the setting as it is, which, I believe, is arguing from the conclusion, WHY can't Chejop, if he decides to commit himself to making Cainan Emperor, preserve his life indefinitely? Or at least for, say, 20-30 years, more than enough time to ensure another worthy successor? He has the Backing of the Bronze Faction and several of the most powerful gods in Heaven, who's going to prevent him from getting some Peaches to preserve stability in Creation? Or are you claiming that the Peaches just wouldn't work? If not, there are other options, the Immortality Hearthstone being one.<br /> <br /> I get that this doesn't work for the setting, it resolves the situation far too easily. I just think 3E should be an opportunity to explain how this works more clearly, by either altering Cainan's situation or suitability for the throne, or (more likely) the game's available Immortality options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T22:02:41-07:00","id":239913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=239902#post239902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, the Bronze <i>can't</i> get Peaches of Immortality or Hearthstones of Immortality for Cathak Cainan or otherwise Kejak's worries about promoting him as a candidate would vanish entirely. Remember, Kejak does not see a worthy successor within House Cathak other than Cainan, and frets that he would be giving the Realm a brief few years of stability before crashing into a second calamitous civil war when Cainan surely dies. One can assume that Cainan is nearing the end of an already extended lifespan already from imperial anagathics (he's roughly 400 years old, after all), and that the Bronze granting their favorite prospect eternal life is off the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>The immortality hearthstone is kinda BS in general, largely because it's boring. I suspect it will be removed in 3e, from previous comments by the devs.<br /> <br /> As for other methods... Yeah, I have to agree with you. If we're to accept that Cainan can't be the front runner because he's going to die from old age roughly when Chejop is, then the Bronze must not be able to further extend his life. Which is something that needs to be taken into account when writing the various anti-agathics in 3e. I'm sure there's a solution here, but it should perhaps be decided on now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T02:17:37-07:00","id":240052,"title":"","content":"I'm sure that if Cathak Cainan suddenly turned up looking eighteen years old, it would turn some heads in a bad way.<br /> <br /> Also, I think there's supposed to be a thing about the Sidereals having already laid down groundwork based on the expectation that Cainan was going to die that it's too late to reverse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T08:23:08-07:00","id":240310,"title":"","content":"Is that how the Peaches work? Even if so, it's still not unworkable: All they have to do is stage the whole thing as a *Gift from the Immaculate Dragons*, a miraculous sign that Cainan is *meant* to be Emperor. Hell, Cainan himself will eat it up, if he's really so pious (I'm unclear if he knows that Sidereals are running the show)!<br /> <br /> The latter reason is actually a much better reason...Still, holding the world together probably merits a few more hours at the office, I would think...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T08:34:56-07:00","id":240327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=239912#post239912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not? Other than to preserve the setting as it is, which, I believe, is arguing from the conclusion, WHY can't Chejop, if he decides to commit himself to making Cainan Emperor, preserve his life indefinitely? Or at least for, say, 20-30 years, more than enough time to ensure another worthy successor? He has the Backing of the Bronze Faction and several of the most powerful gods in Heaven, who's going to prevent him from getting some Peaches to preserve stability in Creation? Or are you claiming that the Peaches just wouldn't work? If not, there are other options, the Immortality Hearthstone being one.<br /> <br /> I get that this doesn't work for the setting, it resolves the situation far too easily. I just think 3E should be an opportunity to explain how this works more clearly, by either altering Cainan's situation or suitability for the throne, or (more likely) the game's available Immortality options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for one thing prolonging the life of a new Emperor is a gross violation of Heavenly law and the Violet Bier of Sorrows is the strongest bailiwick of the Gold Faction. Saturn's Chosen handle internal auditing of the Bureau of Destiny AND matters of fate regarding when things should properly end. If you need an in-game reason for why it's unfeasible, it's not hard to spot one; Kejak would be setting himself up for an enormous indictment and an easy political win for his opposition. And afterwards, Cainan still has to die because that's what's fated.<br /> <br /> As far as the logic goes, &quot;The Bronze can't prolong Cainan's life&quot; is not my conclusion but one of my premises. Kejak's decision-making in Aspect Book: Fire (page 58) makes it clear that Cainan is set to die &quot;soon&quot; and it is not something avoidable. Exalted has plenty of setting facts that appear in contradiction (&quot;Princess V'neef is 60 years old&quot; vs &quot;V'neef Jegan is 300 years old&quot;) but there's a lot of fun to be had in trying to reconcile them. Trying to argue from game-mechanics that setting elements are untrue leads to the Usurpation never happening and neomah breeding farms; its far easier to just decide that particularly annoying crunchy bits, such as the Gem of Immortality, do not invalidate large swathes of written material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T08:39:00-07:00","id":240337,"title":"","content":"All that is justification.<br /> <br /> The reason Sidereals don't make Cathak Cainan immortal is that this cheapens the setting incredibly. The paradox of age and experience, the dilemma of someone who is highly competent but who might die soon and leave everyone in much the same position as they are now, is a compelling, believeable aspect of a succession crisis that can be easily related to real-world history. It's a thing that happens, and it raises interesting problems to explore. Removing it hurts the narrative of the succession crisis more than it brings anything to the table. <br /> <br /> You might as well say that the ideal successor to the Empress is &quot;Mnemon, once Sidereals have used Charm-assisted therapy to make her not a murderous narcissistic sociopath.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T10:49:14-07:00","id":240409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=240310#post240310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All they have to do is stage the whole thing as a *Gift from the Immaculate Dragons*, a miraculous sign that Cainan is *meant* to be Emperor. Hell, Cainan himself will eat it up, if he's really so pious</div> </div> </div> </div>Cathak's piety will leave him questioning how this thing that doesn't fit with the theology of his faith in the slightest is supposed to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T11:28:50-07:00","id":240453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=240409#post240409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how this thing that doesn't fit with the theology of his faith in the slightest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theology, especially a theology explicitly designed to control a nation of supernatural beings, is intentionally vague and can be twisted to many uses. I'd have an easier time backing an argument that preserving the self for the good of the many is against the actions of an Upright Soldier than against the Immaculate doctrine. After all, what is the purpose of Ascetic enlightenment? There would be a way. A way Cainan would accept - maybe not. But a way Peleps Deled would accept, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":1103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","user":"Tikor","date":". 01-03-2020, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T00:48:33-07:00","id":241162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=240409#post240409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cathak's piety will leave him questioning how this thing that doesn't fit with the theology of his faith in the slightest is supposed to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was popularly accepted in the Realm that the Empress was blessed by the five dragons. How would it not fit for her successor to be likewise blessed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T08:17:45-07:00","id":241368,"title":"","content":"Based on my rereading of the Wood Book, I'm pretty sure the best character is Tepet Ejava's mom, aka General &quot;I'm going to carry a pregnancy to labor and then breastfeed my child on the battlefield.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T08:35:56-07:00","id":241376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=241368#post241368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on my rereading of the Wood Book, I'm pretty sure the best character is Tepet Ejava's mom, aka General &quot;I'm going to carry a pregnancy to labor and then breastfeed my child on the battlefield.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And the rest of the Dynasty's reaction is &quot;You nursed your own child? Abhorrent!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T11:51:34-07:00","id":241561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=240453#post240453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a way Pheleps Deled would accept, sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the guy who'll murder you over the difference in opinion of the use of a preposition?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I thought it was popularly accepted in the Realm that the Empress was blessed by the five dragons.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that they'll accept any possible quality she might have as deriving from such blessings, if they run contrary to the aesthetic and philosophical values of the belief system. Otherwise Return of the Scarlet Empress would be a story in which she just passes off her creepy shadow and nemesis powers as blessings from the Immaculate Dragons as well. That's just silly.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T12:24:15-07:00","id":241588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=241368#post241368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on my rereading of the Wood Book, I'm pretty sure the best character is Tepet Ejava's mom, aka General &quot;I'm going to carry a pregnancy to labor and then breastfeed my child on the battlefield.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Ejava's mom was basically The Boss from the Metal Gear Solid franchise? Now in my head canon Ejava wants to be empress because political bull shit lead to her mom becoming an undercover agent and Ejava killing her under orders because those politicians wanted to cover their ass, also she has a wicked cool eye patch.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr