=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Ocelot, so she should be talking about slamming things down well-greased chambers and making weird congratulatory hand gestures before getting a limb cut off and having another major character's arm grafted on, making her allegedly act out like the same. BROTHER!.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't it said that the relationship between Big Boss and The Boss was sort of familial or something like that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T16:26:28-07:00","id":241796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=241775#post241775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't it said that the relationship between Big Boss and The Boss was sort of familial or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sorrow was the father.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T13:51:18-07:00","id":242524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=241588#post241588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, Ejava's mom was basically The Boss from the Metal Gear Solid franchise? Now in my head canon Ejava wants to be empress because political bull shit lead to her mom becoming an undercover agent and Ejava killing her under orders because those politicians wanted to cover their ass, also she has a wicked cool eye patch.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or instead...<br /> <br /> <i>Yes ma'am. The entire talon was wiped out. Those two are still alive. The vector? Yes ma'am, the Contagion should become activated soon... Right on schedule.<br /> <br /> Yes, ma'am. I recovered the Thousand Forged Dragon blueprints... No, ma'am. My cover is intact. Nobody knows who I really am. Yes, the Prefect knew my identity, but he's been disposed of.<br /> <br /> Yes. Thank you. Good-bye. Mrs. Shogun.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T18:30:18-07:00","id":242736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=241368#post241368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on my rereading of the Wood Book, I'm pretty sure the best character is Tepet Ejava's mom, aka General &quot;I'm going to carry a pregnancy to labor and then breastfeed my child on the battlefield.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>...and then you find out that Ejava is a fifth child, and the first four died during exactly this sort of behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1165-hecaton","name":"Hecaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T18:58:57-07:00","id":242765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=238725#post238725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Because the narrator fears Bhagwei would dismantle the Realm's empire out of humanitarian concern?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always read it as the narrator believing that Ragara Bhagwei's virtue would be destroyed by the necessities of running the Realm, because often the very best available choices in empire management, even dismantlement, are merely between great evils.<br /> <br /> Consider the four British decolonizations under the postwar Labour government of Clement Attlee. Continued British rule could have been only maintained through significant amounts of bloodshed. But the end of British rule did not mean the end of bloodshed. There was the decolonization of India, which was followed by three Indo-Pakistani wars and now a Cold War in miniature of nuclear-armed states and terror attacks. There was the decolonization of Palestine, with results that have been appearing in headlines all this summer. There's the decolonization of Sri Lanka, which resulted in unrest, riots, institutionalized racism, and a 25-year civil war. And then there's the decolonization of Burma, which has had essentially constant civil wars since, and an oppressive military junta for decades. Complain that Clement Attlee mismanaged all four and something better could have been done if you like, the better still likely would have been soaked in the blood of thousands.<br /> <br /> Could a man of genuine deep compassion have a hand in that sort of thing without either coarsening or going mad? Trade fifty thousand deaths in one place and time for twenty thousand elsewhere and elsewhen, and you still have condemned thousands that would have lived had you taken the first course. If you do anything but close yourself off from that horror, how do you remain sane? If you do close yourself off from it, how can you do anything but dim your own compassion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T13:42:07-07:00","id":244976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=239869#post239869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, reading Mnemon's SoE write-up, she has a Stone of Immortality. Is this original to that book? ISTR reading that her unusual youth/lifespan was due to [...] trying to duplicate her mother's agelessness</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll notice that in Her Redness's write up, there's no mention of what keeps her young... other than the possibility of having manse 5. But sure, in her orginal write up Little Red didn't have the Immortality Gemstone (or a hearthstone slot in her armour).<br /> <br /> I like the idea of it being hearthstones that keep them young. Lends credence to RotSE. Lords of Creation (plus everything ever written about hearthstones) implies that 5 dotters are really rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T19:28:06-07:00","id":245138,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it might not be a mistake to put in too many implications that there's something sinister and mysterious about the longevity and vitality of characters like Mnemon and the Scarlet Empress. For one thing, the tone and details of the setting feel like something that supports the idea that, if you're sufficiently wealthy and well connected, and have good fortune in the genes department, it's not especially difficult to access resources that can extend your lifespan. I'd also think that, even if it's not directly detailed, it wouldn't be difficult to figure out how to make a sorcerous project to aid in such. Mnemon and the Empress are well endowed with all such things to among the highest levels*, and it isn't really a big deal, it's just part of the general strangeness.<br /> <br /> For Cainan, I'd say he's in the genetic bad luck and not entirely healthy lifestyle department, and is insufficiently motivated to acquire the resources to live notably longer. Sidereals look on this, and mostly just shrug at what a shame it is; it would be convenient if he was going to live longer, but not to a degree sufficient to invest a lot of effort towards preserving him. A Peach of Immortality is actually the last thing you want to put in that situation, or any other for that matter; they're such a valuable commodity in Yu-Shan that their acquisition and transportation is not only extremely expensive, but a security nightmare, and they're so beyond valuable in Creation that hardly any figure they could save will provide a contribution sufficient to outweigh the likely degree of violence over possession of one if word of them should get out. Heck, if you offered Cainan a Peach of Immortality, and he fully understood what it was, there's a good chance he'd either hoard it against some future possibilities (which is fairly likely to end with him being murdered by a retainer or family member in the course of them stealing it), or sell it for the sake of resources he can use towards certain more immediate gratifications (which then means you've let a Peach of Immortality out to cause chaos in the world). The fact of their value and their rarity alone is the kind of thing that will often create an aversion to eating one immediately just for the sake of having it around, even if this isn't rational (although, on the other hand, there's something to be said for holding off on it for as long as possible for the sake of extending your life to the fullest degree).<br /> <br /> That's not to say that your characters can't engage in the expense and undertake the risks (which are reasonably manageable within the setting) to actually acquire, transport and consume the things, but it's part of why people generally wouldn't try in the setting. It's really the sort of audacious thing that can be left open for PCs who want to take a crack at it, rather than something just assumed to be lined up and easy outside of the circles of the game. <br /> <br /> * I imagine that for a lot of other people, the options within reach might not be quite so dignified. Ragara is almost twice as old as Mnemon is, but whatever his methods and advantages, they don't quite seem to have kept him in the best condition, although that might just be bad luck or some differences in lifestyle. I imagine there are a fair number of Dynasts who succumb to old age even when they could make a crack at living a lot longer because they don't care for the alteration in how they'd leave the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T19:47:27-07:00","id":245146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div 