sion of one if word of them should get out. Heck, if you offered Cainan a Peach of Immortality, and he fully understood what it was, there's a good chance he'd either hoard it against some future possibilities (which is fairly likely to end with him being murdered by a retainer or family member in the course of them stealing it), or sell it for the sake of resources he can use towards certain more immediate gratifications (which then means you've let a Peach of Immortality out to cause chaos in the world). The fact of their value and their rarity alone is the kind of thing that will often create an aversion to eating one immediately just for the sake of having it around, even if this isn't rational (although, on the other hand, there's something to be said for holding off on it for as long as possible for the sake of extending your life to the fullest degree).<br /> <br /> That's not to say that your characters can't engage in the expense and undertake the risks (which are reasonably manageable within the setting) to actually acquire, transport and consume the things, but it's part of why people generally wouldn't try in the setting. It's really the sort of audacious thing that can be left open for PCs who want to take a crack at it, rather than something just assumed to be lined up and easy outside of the circles of the game.<br /> <br /> * I imagine that for a lot of other people, the options within reach might not be quite so dignified. Ragara is almost twice as old as Mnemon is, but whatever his methods and advantages, they don't quite seem to have kept him in the best condition, although that might just be bad luck or some differences in lifestyle. I imagine there are a fair number of Dynasts who succumb to old age even when they could make a crack at living a lot longer because they don't care for the alteration in how they'd leave the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I usually forget Ragara is still alive since he has no setting impact anymore. He honestly might as well be dead if the only reason they keep him around is as a footnote for showing that exalted can get senile to if they live too long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T00:30:19-07:00","id":245214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=245146#post245146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I usually forget Ragara is still alive since he has no setting impact anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much of the Scarlet Dynasty do you forget?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He honestly might as well be dead if the only reason they keep him around is as a footnote for showing that exalted can get senile to if they live too long.</div> </div> </div> </div>O....kay...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T01:04:35-07:00","id":245222,"title":"","content":"I kind of forgot Ragara is around as well. And to be fair, Ragara retired to some island and is doing fuck all. Unlike Mnemon or even Cainan, Ragara hasn't been presented as doing much of anything important in the current setting and hardly gets a mention in the gameline. <br /> <br /> In fact, thinking about it, the only time I remember him getting much of a mention was in one of the scenarios back in 1st edition Alchemicals, where his murder by the Alchemicals helped kickstart the war between Autochthonia and the Realm into overdrive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T01:13:05-07:00","id":245229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How much of the Scarlet Dynasty do you forget? </div> </div> </div><br /> That is a hard question to answer, it is kinda hard to keep track of the number of things you have forgotten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T04:04:01-07:00","id":245272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=241368#post241368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on my rereading of the Wood Book, I'm pretty sure the best character is Tepet Ejava's mom, aka General &quot;I'm going to carry a pregnancy to labor and then breastfeed my child on the battlefield.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sure, but I like to think that Sesus 'I'll hold together half the Realm's political structure despite being hated and crippled' Nagezzer is equal. Not better. Just equal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T07:59:59-07:00","id":245332,"title":"","content":"I read John's answer to the &quot;Give Cainan a Peach!&quot; sitch, that 3E will assume that the PoI aren't exactly laying around so that anyone could get one...which honestly strikes me as a rather facetious answer. Those things are certainly not portrayed that way in previous editions, and are under heavy divine guard at all times!<br /> <br /> Also, Chejop, THE prime example of the Chosen of the Maidens in the eyes of many Gods, is hardly just anybody, or some nobody. Isator comes up with an interesting in-setting rationale, but given that we're talking about THE most politically important people in the setting (as opposed to narratively important, which are your PCs), I really don't see anyone putting up more than token resistance to him requistioning one or more to give to the one man almost guaranteed to stop the largest empire in the world, on which the Bronze Faction has placed all its hopes, extended life. And uniting the Realm is *certainly* worth the possible danger of bringing a peach to earth!<br /> <br /> Not that they have to do so: It is well within the capabilities of Sids and their godly allies to stage a heavenly visitation of the sort that Paul and Muhammad underwent...in fact, it's not even staged, they literally CAN &quot;spirit away&quot; Cainan to Yu-Shan, dazzle him with the wonders of Heaven, and have Elemental Dragons in the guise of the Immaculates give him a persuasive speech about how Special he is, how they have been moved to act through their infinite compassion for the Realm, etc, and eat of this peach and we will deliver the throne onto you...He doesn't have any opportunity to squirrel it away for later. <br /> <br /> (This is assuming they did this intelligently, of course. If they hold a meeting about how to pull this off, well...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Incidentally, where are the Peaches written up? I thought they were in the Peach Orchards section of Yu-Shan compass, but nope! Exactly what do they do for one who eats one? I'm guessing their name is an exaggeration. For that matter, even if they DID grant immortality, they'd still be pretty useless to the already immortal gods, so...what's the point of them, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T08:07:26-07:00","id":245334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=241561#post241561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cathak's piety will leave him questioning how this thing that doesn't fit with the theology of his faith in the slightest is supposed to work.Cathak's piety will leave him questioning how this thing that doesn't fit with the theology of his faith in the slightest is supposed to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plenty of less pious folks in RL commit actions or follow causes that conflict with the theology of their faith (&quot;&quot;Thou Shall Not Kill&quot; clearly doesn't apply to blowing up this abortion clinic!&quot;) without having their actual gods show up and confirm how exceptional they are that they don't have to follow those rules; and Chejop can arrange for that to (seem to) happen.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That doesn't mean that they'll accept any possible quality she might have as deriving from such blessings, if they run contrary to the aesthetic and philosophical values of the belief system. Otherwise Return of the Scarlet Empress would be a story in which she just passes off her creepy shadow and nemesis powers as blessings from the Immaculate Dragons as well. That's just silly.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> </div> </div> </div>True. But what if Cainan's ascension is accompanied by *actual Elemental displays* in the sky, accomplished by Lesser Elemental Dragons? And we've seen that the Immaculate Order will preach whatever Chejop tells them to, so when they start constantly spouting off support for him, most of the masses will be predisposed to go along with it. <br /> <br /> Also, help me out, but which exact values of the Order would be defied here?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T11:20:03-07:00","id":245492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, where are the Peaches written up? I thought they were in the Peach Orchards section of Yu-Shan compass, but nope! Exactly what do they do for one who eats one? I'm guessing their name is an exaggeration.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're in Exalted: the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> A peach takes three bites to eat. One bite will remove a decade from the age of a mortal or Terrestrial, and a century from a Celestial. A whole peach eaten in one sitting will return a mortal or Terrestrial to the beginning of adulthood, and removes up to a millenium from a Celestial. Eating further peaches will have no more effect until a year has passed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter, even if they DID grant immortality, they'd still be pretty useless to the already immortal gods, so...what's the point of them, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're luxuriantly tasty.<br /> <br /> Possibly also a reference to the Well of Immortality of Tanith Lee's Upperearth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T11:32:55-07:00","id":245517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=245492#post245492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're in Exalted: the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> A peach takes three bites to eat. One bite will remove a decade from the age of a mortal or Terrestrial, and a century from a Celestial. A whole peach eaten in one sitting will return a mortal or Terrestrial to the beginning of adulthood, and removes up to a millenium from a Celestial. Eating further peaches will have no more effect until a year has passed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'll have to dig that out, I'm guessing Celestial Wine is in there, too...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're luxuriantly tasty.<br /> <br /> Possibly also a reference to the Well of Immortality of Tanith Lee's Upperearth. </div> </div> </div>Not to the Peaches stolen by the Monkey King? <br /> <br /> Either way, I'm liking the idea of a Scourge sneaking into heaven to steal a few to take to earth, explicitly to cause the very chaos you describe! Sort of a cross between the Monkey King story and the Apple of Discord...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T01:34:47-08:00","id":1358157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=244976#post244976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll notice that in Her Redness's write up, there's no mention of what keeps her young... other than the possibility of having manse 5. But sure, in her orginal write up Little Red didn't have the Immortality Gemstone (or a hearthstone slot in her armour).<br /> <br /> I like the idea of it being hearthstones that keep them young. Lends credence to RotSE. Lords of Creation (plus everything ever written about hearthstones) implies that 5 dotters are really rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for reference, in WFHW it mentions the Empress wears a burning Hearthstone (and a pair of others) that her kin would murder her for.<br /> <br /> My reading is the burning Hearthstone is linked to the Imperial Manse (and may or may not be the source of her longevity), but what other Hearthstones are rare and powerful enough to drive Dynasts to Matricide?<br /> <br /> I'm heavily leaning toward Gem of Immortality here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T03:33:48-08:00","id":1358168,"title":"","content":"So yeah. Bhagwei. Dude's a poorly written jerk and I hate his guts and don't remotely get what you guys see in him.<br /> <br /> Granted, I mostly hate his guts because of his actions as master of the Heptagram. But taking a step back here, let's consider how stupid his story in Aspect Book Wood is on every level. The secret incest baby thing comes off like the writer just discovered Game of Thrones for the first time and was feeling all edgy and hardcore (this is early White Wolf after all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) The most baffling part however is how completely irrelevant it is to Bhagwei's story. It's basically there to give him a claim to the throne... so he can ignore it and be all 'I'm too good for secular power'. You really didn't need incest to give the guy who personally trained almost every active sorcerer in the Realm a claim to the throne. So yeah, not only incest, but stupid pointless incest there to make us be more disgusted at the Dynasty. Yaaaay.<br /> <br /> (It's small potatoes compared to that and what comes next, but the Empress killing her newly healed lover is also very stupid. I get that it's supposed to be subversive, remind us 'oh yeah, the dynasty are the bad guys' but it didn't have that vibe to me at all. It just felt stupid, a capricious act to try and shock me, the reader.)<br /> <br /> So yeah. Following that, we get the high crimes stuff. Ragara Bhagwei, dominie of the Heptagram, takes advantage of his position to initiate a sexual relationship with a student, Tepet Oshina. Due to the course of these 'experiments', she is killed.<br /> <br /> *breath*<br /> <br /> You guys are gonna fan for this? Really?<br /> <br /> Because that's my biggest issue with the point. Yes, it's sodding tasteless in isolation. But the presentation of it is what runs beyond irksome into frothing anger for me. The book seemingly, <b>bafflingly </b>doesn't regard this as a villain moment. There's a sidebar <i>encouraging PCs to continue these experiments</i>. It's one rejoinder is that PCs &quot; should opt to begin their experiments with bisclaverets or neomah as guinea pigs instead of the daughter of a powerful Great House!&quot; The tone reads as comedic to me - as if Bhagwei doing this to the daughter of a Great House was the one mistake he made. Bhagwei is not an obviously unreliable narrator like Deled, he's presented as more detached and analytical, and he's given an excuse that Oshina hadn't done the preparations he'd asked of her. Further the text sets her up with mild slutshaming, Bhagwei noting her &quot;appetite for rich, old Exalts near death from old age&quot;. Painting her as a gold digger to try and ensure the reader isn't sympathetic to her fate.<br /> <br /> The whole passage isn't written like the act of a villain, it's just 'a thing that happened'. And yeah, that's kinda opinion. But look at the OP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ragara Bhagwei knows the ways to sex so powerful, it makes his Dragon-Blooded partners <i>explode</i>. He usually refrains. </div> </div> </div>And I'm not trying to get at Omicron here, just use their words for illustrative effect. That's <i>absolutely </i>how this bit was written. It's not given gravity akin to Deled's fanaticism, or Lahor's brutality. Bhagwei is presented as a 'good Dynast', fighting Abyssals and being aloof from politics. .<br /> <br /> Oh, and lest we forget, he then proceeds to skin a little girl and wear her as magic clothing.<br /> <br /> ... I'd be lying if I said that disgusts me as much as I find it... grimly hilarious, in the 'wise old sorcerer' writeup. It definitely helps me not be able to take him seriously as any kind of positive, goodly mentor figure? I'd rather use Sesus Chenow in that role - at least I can try and argue old age mellowed him out a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4086,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","user":"Croakamancer","date":". 01-01-2020, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T04:14:17-08:00","id":1358176,"title":"","content":"First time I read Aspect Book Wood I had an idea for a ghost story in the Heptagram. It would turn out that the experiment had been successful and the &quot;ghost&quot; was Tepet Oshina's still-living essence pattern trying to reconstitute. I never did anything with it because I realised the payoff would bank heavily on my players having read Aspect Book Wood to appreciate the twist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T09:36:51-08:00","id":1358211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=239889#post239889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wanna say that AB: Earth claimed she stopped aging after the Versino exploded, but that might just be a faulty memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went through to the end just to make sure I didn't see this answered. And I'm pretty sure I didn't, so...<br /> <br /> That was something in 2e, I'm pretty sure. 1e said that she at least publicly attributed her longevity to emulation of the dragons, but I don't recall if it was explicit in why she had never moved into her middle age.<br /> <br /> Her apparent age was a definite change, though, from 1e to 2e. 1e's aspect book description said she looked to be in her thirties, and 2e, at least once, described her as looking like an eternal teenager, never aging past her days in secondary school, and explicitly went with the &quot;stopped aging once the Versino exploded.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T09:48:25-08:00","id":1358212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1358164#post1358164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... John, you don't come across like you're interested in <i>debate </i>or like you respect my opinion when you start taking shots like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologise for any offense caused. My intent was only to contextualize the conversation -- wasn't meant as a personal attack. Likewise I'm sure your points should be read as criticism of the work and not of the writers or fans of the character. I'm notoriously bad for conveying meaning -- just had an argument with someone in Ask a Question whom I agreed with in every respect. So let me kick this off with &quot;my bad&quot;, and &quot;I'm sorry&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356534-let-s-read-the-aspect-books?p=1358164#post1358164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your points, as far as I can tell, don't remotely track with any of my complaints. But eh. Let's adjourn to that other thread. You've already necromancied it, I feel like cutting loose 100%</div> </div> </div> </div>Those points weren't really meant to track with what you said. It was just my take on the character -- didn't want to argue in someone else's active thread.<br /> <br /> That said, I think most of your criticism is valid. You're entitled to your interpretation and opinion. It's different to mine but I respect your right to hold it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358168#post1358168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah. Bhagwei. Dude's a poorly written jerk and I hate his guts and don't remotely get what you guys see in him.<br /> <br /> Granted, I mostly hate his guts because of his actions as master of the Heptagram. But taking a step back here, let's consider how stupid his story in Aspect Book Wood is on every level. The secret incest baby thing comes off like the writer just discovered Game of Thrones for the first time and was feeling all edgy and hardcore (this is early White Wolf after all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) The most baffling part however is how completely irrelevant it is to Bhagwei's story. It's basically there to give him a claim to the throne... so he can ignore it and be all 'I'm too good for secular power'. You really didn't need incest to give the guy who personally trained almost every active sorcerer in the Realm a claim to the throne. So yeah, not only incest, but stupid pointless incest there to make us be more disgusted at the Dynasty. Yaaaay.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong.<br /> <br /> But why make Mnemon the daughter of the Empress? Why not have her be the second most powerful sorceress and leader of a politically powerful block?<br /> <br /> Because it's a dynasty. In real life as well as fantasy, royal bloodlines and inheritance are important. Political power needs to be backed by a claim. (If we're talking Game of Thrones, Rob became king because he had a blood claim which Ned lacked.)<br /> <br /> And sexual deviance is House Cynis's whole thing (well that and slavery).<br /> <br /> The Dynasty aren't nice people. They're twisted, imperialistic, slaveholders... who are also the foremost heroes of Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358168#post1358168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(It's small potatoes compared to that and what comes next, but the Empress killing her newly healed lover is also very stupid. I get that it's supposed to be subversive, remind us 'oh yeah, the dynasty are the bad guys' but it didn't have that vibe to me at all. It just felt stupid, a capricious act to try and shock me, the reader.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Empress gives her reasoning here.<br /> <br /> She expects the lover to die -- given what we know of Mnemon's lovers, it's probable the Empress poisoned her herself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358168#post1358168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah. Following that, we get the high crimes stuff. Ragara Bhagwei, dominie of the Heptagram, takes advantage of his position to initiate a sexual relationship with a student, Tepet Oshina. Due to the course of these 'experiments', she is killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. The Dean of Magic College abuses his power and asplodes a student.<br /> <br /> Sex and politics is what a Dynastic game is all about. Throw in a little magic and death and you've got yourself a Heptagram game.<br /> <br /> It's evil. It's full on Guide to the Sabbat, trench-coat and katana evil.<br /> <br /> That's why it's fun.<br /> <br /> It's not fun for everyone. Some people are going to be upset or disturbed by this. Like any group activity, basic human decency means you need to treat the other players with respect when dealing with these sorts of themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358168#post1358168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*breath*<br /> <br /> You guys are gonna fan for this? Really?<br /> <br /> Because that's my biggest issue with the point. Yes, it's sodding tasteless in isolation. But the presentation of it is what runs beyond irksome into frothing anger for me. The book seemingly, <b>bafflingly </b>doesn't regard this as a villain moment. There's a sidebar <i>encouraging PCs to continue these experiments</i>. It's one rejoinder is that PCs &quot; should opt to begin their experiments with bisclaverets or neomah as guinea pigs instead of the daughter of a powerful Great House!&quot; The tone reads as comedic to me - as if Bhagwei doing this to the daughter of a Great House was the one mistake he made. Bhagwei is not an obviously unreliable narrator like Deled, he's presented as more detached and analytical, and he's given an excuse that Oshina hadn't done the preparations he'd asked of her. Further the text sets her up with mild slutshaming, Bhagwei noting her &quot;appetite for rich, old Exalts near death from old age&quot;. Painting her as a gold digger to try and ensure the reader isn't sympathetic to her fate.<br /> <br /> The whole passage isn't written like the act of a villain, it's just 'a thing that happened'. And yeah, that's kinda opinion. But look at the OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solars aren't Lawful Good to Realm Chaotic Evil.<br /> <br /> But the Realm are the default bad guys. Your Realm PCs are evil and need evil plot hooks. <br /> <br /> &quot;My Realm PC isn't evil! They just benefit from a system of slavery and war!&quot;<br /> <br /> Well good news! This sex magic isn't just exploding people for fun -- it's a practical study of mysticism!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358168#post1358168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm not trying to get at Omicron here, just use their words for illustrative effect. That's <i>absolutely </i>how this bit was written. It's not given gravity akin to Deled's fanaticism, or Lahor's brutality. Bhagwei is presented as a 'good Dynast', fighting Abyssals and being aloof from politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bhaghwei was written to appeal to the people he appeals to. He's exactly what I want from a mythic hero in a game with questionable morality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358168#post1358168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and lest we forget, he then proceeds to skin a little girl and wear her as magic clothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better or worse than a Lunar ripping out her heart to drink of its blood?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358168#post1358168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I'd be lying if I said that disgusts me as much as I find it... grimly hilarious, in the 'wise old sorcerer' writeup. It definitely helps me not be able to take him seriously as any kind of positive, goodly mentor figure? I'd rather use Sesus Chenow in that role - at least I can try and argue old age mellowed him out a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how magic works.<br /> <br /> Want to summon a Blood Ape? Murder a cat. Want a courtesan? Trade flesh for flesh. Looking to destroy your enemies? Rain poison down upon the land.<br /> <br /> A &quot;wise old sorcerer&quot; is a lot closer to Voldemont than Dumbledore.<br /> <br /> I want my characters morally ambiguous at best. Especially my Dynasts. The things that seem to turn you off are the things needed to counterbalance Bhagwei so he doesn't outshine the PCs.<br /> <br /> Bhagwei the White as a shining paragon of good, curing the great contagion, teaching Dynasts to use sorcery responsibly, solving crises between peach bites, with a good claim to the throne? Blah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 01-01-2020, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T09:54:18-08:00","id":1358215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358212#post1358212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's evil. It's full on Guide to the Sabbat, trench-coat and katana evil.<br /> <br /> That's why it's fun.<br /> <br /> It's not fun for everyone. Some people are going to be upset or disturbed by this. Like any group activity, basic human decency means you need to treat the other players with respect when dealing with these sorts of themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thus, I heartily recommend that if someone doesn't like that aspect of the setting, treat it as wholly villainous on your own.<br /> Parading about it doesn't achieve much, and I'd rather not err on the side of sanitizing anything remotely playable. Villainous heroes and heroic villains are a necessity in a world that has both good, evil, and heroes, and expects you to be on either side of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T10:29:45-08:00","id":1358219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358215#post1358215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thus, I heartily recommend that if someone doesn't like that aspect of the setting, treat it as wholly villainous on your own.<br /> Parading about it doesn't achieve much, and I'd rather not err on the side of sanitizing anything remotely playable. Villainous heroes and heroic villains are a necessity in a world that has both good, evil, and heroes, and expects you to be on either side of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. <br /> <br /> Raski literally eats babies but is the &quot;default&quot; wise old wizard mentor for Lunars.<br /> <br /> Everyone is the hero of their own story. And the villian of someone else's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 01-01-2020, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T14:31:28-08:00","id":1358256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358219#post1358219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Everyone </b>is the hero of their own story. And the villian of someone else's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily; some people manage to muddle through their stories without giving much thought to morality or heroism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T15:17:38-08:00","id":1358270,"title":"","content":"Bhagwei is interesting because he manages to do some fairly disgusting and horrifying things, while honestly being almost certainly a net force for good in the world. The book outright admits that he is a megalomaniac with a messiah complex, but his whole thing is curing diseases. Really, how many elder Dynasts are there who would personally visit a small town to cure all the diseased mortals? You probably wouldn't want to hang around him if you weren't sick, though.<br /> <br /> Skinning the Shoat of the Mire is a pretty disturbing thing to do, but let us keep in mind that from his perspective, he was dealing with a monstrous demon that merely happened to resemble a little girl. It's fucking gross, but who did he hurt exactly? (I mean, other than the Shoat herself. But he and his bodyguards were hardly obligated to concern themselves with the deathknight's tragic backstory while she was trying her damnedest to kill them.) From a detached perspective (probably normal for Exalted sorcerers), he's just making use of available resources after winning that fight.<br /> <br /> Killing one of his students with careless tantric experiments is pretty goddamn inexcusable, though. I'm guessing the Scarlet Realm doesn't have the same taboos against sex between people in imbalanced power situations that we do IRL...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T15:31:40-08:00","id":1358274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358270#post1358270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing the Scarlet Realm doesn't have the same taboos against sex between people in imbalanced power situations that we do IRL...</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt the Empress would have had half as many consorts as she is said to have had, if it did.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T15:37:06-08:00","id":1358278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358274#post1358274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt the Empress would have had half as many consorts as she is said to have had, if it did.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, she was the <i>Empress</i> and she had her finger on the big red button of the Sword of Creation. Even if society generally disapproved of that sort of thing, who was going to tell her to stop?<br /> <br /> (Although, the very fact of the Empress doing it so much probably contributed to it <i>being</i> acceptable.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T16:34:45-08:00","id":1358301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358270#post1358270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killing one of his students with careless tantric experiments is pretty goddamn inexcusable, though. I'm guessing the Scarlet Realm doesn't have the same taboos against sex between people in imbalanced power situations that we do IRL...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm doesn't present itself as having a culture of (for lack of a better word) pederasty that normalises and even romanticises such behaviour, it still appears to be a taboo practice. Just one that people with enough power flaunt or participate in to gain leverage on someone who thought they were using them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T17:01:36-08:00","id":1358307,"title":"","content":"If that kind of thing is hard for you to look past then the shocking racism of basically everyone is probably going to put you off most of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T17:35:29-08:00","id":1358311,"title":"","content":"Tribalism, not racism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T18:52:26-08:00","id":1358324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358307#post1358307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that kind of thing is hard for you to look past then the shocking racism of basically everyone is probably going to put you off most of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's often less a reaction towards the setting and more what ideas authors might be perpetuating (even unknowingly) through the medium.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T19:12:58-08:00","id":1358326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358311#post1358311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tribalism, not racism.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I don't really know how much better that is. The ministry of the Bursars of Barbarian Tribute might be considered offensive, and it might be even more offensive when everyone that you voice that to doesn't understand what the big deal is.<br /> <br /> It's not just the Realm either, if you try to bring up bringing security and liberty to all the people that the Bull of the North's armies come across it wouldn't even be considered amusing so much as provoke profound confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T19:49:38-08:00","id":1358334,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s better - we\u2019re still pre-judging people for factors over which they have no control - just that the distinction is important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T19:57:54-08:00","id":1358337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358334#post1358334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not saying it\u2019s better - we\u2019re still pre-judging people for factors over which they have no control - just that the distinction is important.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case what is the important distinction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T20:07:20-08:00","id":1358340,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll talk about it when I don\u2019t have two minutes to clock in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T00:03:19-08:00","id":1358363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358301#post1358301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm doesn't present itself as having a culture of (for lack of a better word) pederasty that normalises and even romanticises such behaviour, it still appears to be a taboo practice. Just one that people with enough power flaunt or participate in to gain leverage on someone who thought they were using them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't it?<br /> <br /> One of the Chapter fictions in WFHW is about pedastry in the Realm. Secondary School kids (18+) seem to be sexually active with each other. There's at least one teacher at the <s>Stair</s> House of Ancient Stone who takes it easy on his young male lovers. I've always played the Realm as quite... Athenian?<br /> <br /> Paedophilia is a hard taboo.<br /> <br /> Adults having sex with young adults (late teens) is well established.<br /> <br /> Bhagwei killing his young lover is clearly taboo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 01-03-2020, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T01:51:24-08:00","id":1358377,"title":"","content":"I didn't get the impression that his lover was a child. The older Heptagram students are basically university students, so in their 20s. (Obviously he's much older, but she's not a child.)<br /> <br /> Not to say there might not be rules saying that teachers can't have sex with students, but whether there's a culture of pederasty or not isn't really necessary for them to think teachers sleeping with adult students is okay.<br /> <br /> Killing your student clearly is not though. I imagine that was covered up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T03:07:08-08:00","id":1358384,"title":"","content":"I don't have my books with me. So the only instance I can recall where it was heavily implied to be a problem was Tepet Lisara's backstory with her blackmailing multiple instructors.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T04:11:17-08:00","id":1358393,"title":"","content":"Double post because it's an unrelated line of thought.<br /> <br /> Given the direction of House Ragara in 3rd edition as not just the money house but by introducing the sinister occult research of its Inner Circle there's going to be some recontextualising of Bhagwei especially with his relationship with Banoba.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T05:30:56-08:00","id":1358399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358337#post1358337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case what is the important distinction?</div> </div> </div> </div>The distinction is that race is a fabricated notion, one that luckily hasn\u2019t gelled in Creation the way it has in our world. Panther isn\u2019t treated differently when he strolls into town because of his black skin; he\u2019s treated differently because he\u2019s a stranger, because of his Nexus accent, and because few in the community he\u2019s wandered into have ever encountered such a hulking, tattooed giant of a gladiator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T07:26:02-08:00","id":1358413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358399#post1358399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The distinction is that race is a fabricated notion, one that luckily hasn\u2019t gelled in Creation the way it has in our world. Panther isn\u2019t treated differently when he strolls into town because of his black skin; he\u2019s treated differently because he\u2019s a stranger, because of his Nexus accent, and because few in the community he\u2019s wandered into have ever encountered such a hulking, tattooed giant of a gladiator.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I thought for sure there\u2019d be stigma among people on the Blessed Isle attached to looking like you\u2019re from Halta or some other place that\u2019s designated barbarous.<br /> <br /> Then again maybe there\u2019s just black and white Dynasts and everywhere has a big mix of skin tones, hair colour and facial features. Either way the Realm, and most places in the world, are not cool with linking hands and being at peace with and respectful of everyone else\u2019s cultures. I mean, nobody in the real world is like that anyway. If you think you are just remember there\u2019s some cultures that consider it right and proper to bury an adulteress up to her neck in sand and hurl stones at her head until she dies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 01-02-2020, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T07:54:29-08:00","id":1358418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358413#post1358413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I thought for sure there\u2019d be stigma among people on the Blessed Isle attached to looking like you\u2019re from Halta or some other place that\u2019s designated barbarous.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, to the Realm, everywhere that's <i>not</i> the Realm is &quot;barbaric.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358413#post1358413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again maybe there\u2019s just black and white Dynasts and everywhere has a big mix of skin tones, hair colour and facial features.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's in the 3e Core book that no one region of Creation is <i>completely</i> dominated by a single skin tone; constant trade leads to people being transplanted. They're not as common, but there <b>are </b>Dynasts with dark skin, and rare light-skinned people in the Burning Sands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-02-2020, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T08:22:34-08:00","id":1358420,"title":"","content":"I've got mixed feelings on Bhagwei. Interesting character, but does seem to have some baked special-for specialness sake. The peach-juice miracle by bureaucracy thing? That just felt ...ehh... like he's the master of 1K Realm Sorcerers /and/ he single handedly solved a bureaucracy problem that a dozen other leading Dynast DB's thought impossible? Oh, and he's also too special and kind to want the Throne? On a certain level it kinda reeks. Anyway! Not a 100% nitpick, I do mostly like the character.<br /> <br /> As for racism/tribalism/the Realm; given the contexts of power in Creation is lined up along Exaltation and spirit patronage rather than access to material resources and adaptations (guns, germs, steel) like the real world; it makes total sense that melanin and minor facial features would mean little in Creation. Racism features due to an outgrowth of advantage, which is itself an outgrowth of where we come from. If any region might spawn a sibling Dragon to homogenize with the differences of ethnic racism become all the less.<br /> <br /> At least, I'm sure that's how it feels to an outsider of the Dynasty, whereas the boarding school atmosphere of the Dynasty Schools likely look for every possible minor difference to draw out and create cliques from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T11:24:20-08:00","id":1358453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358168#post1358168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah. Bhagwei. Dude's a poorly written jerk and I hate his guts and don't remotely get what you guys see in him.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>... How did you find this thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T13:12:58-08:00","id":1358469,"title":"","content":"He didn't, JohnDoe raised it from its digital grave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T13:16:40-08:00","id":1358473,"title":"","content":"I need more bed rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T18:18:55-08:00","id":1358510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358413#post1358413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again maybe there\u2019s just black and white Dynasts and everywhere has a big mix of skin tones, hair colour and facial features.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it helps to remember that the Dynasty isn't derived from the natives of the Blessed Isle* it's derived from the Shogunate remnants who swore loyality to the Scarlet Empress.<br /> <br /> *which if old lore still stands had no native human population prior to the Primordial War so is a melting pot of its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T18:26:25-08:00","id":1358512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358473#post1358473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need more bed rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't we all...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T20:58:29-08:00","id":1358538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358510#post1358510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it helps to remember that the Dynasty isn't derived from the natives of the Blessed Isle* it's derived from the Shogunate remnants who swore loyality to the Scarlet Empress.<br /> <br /> *which if old lore still stands had no native human population prior to the Primordial War so is a melting pot of its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh true, isn't there also some new lore about Blessed Isle natives not getting along well with the Shogunate remnant cultures that populate most of the isle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T02:42:12-08:00","id":1358575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358363#post1358363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the Chapter fictions in WFHW is about pedastry in the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eshuvar doesn't exactly seem to have the sympathy of Realm society which seems to want him to grow the fuck up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's at least one teacher at the Stair who takes it easy on his young male lovers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're thinking of the guy who runs the House of the Ancient Stone. But regardless. Exalted books have frequently presented NPCs in terms of what's interesting about them rather than knowledge they'd openly volunteer about themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T05:26:46-08:00","id":1358594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358453#post1358453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... How did you find this thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whilst I unCroaked this thread with Croakamancer in mind (neither one of us wanted to clutter DrLoveMonkey's thread, and this thread is one of my bookmarks), I did bump it (possibly against forum ettiquet, apologies Lioness) with a post about the possibility of the Empress's longevity being the result of having a Gemstone of Immortality.<br /> <br /> Which is something I'm interested in discussing further if anyone else is interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T05:37:10-08:00","id":1358598,"title":"","content":"Sure, it\u2019s possible, but to me, it\u2019s the least interesting option.<br /> <br /> Consider, for instance, the sorts of limits to immortality provided by sorcerous workings. What might she be doing, to sustain her unnatural longevity? Or perhaps there\u2019s a potent god out there granting her extended years; what might she owe him, and is her recent disappearance his attempt to collect a debt? Maybe her advanced age is the result of an unprecedented change in nature to the Dragon-Blooded\u2019s inner fire, and clever players might deduce means for themselves to do the same?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-03-2020, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T05:46:24-08:00","id":1358603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358594#post1358594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whilst I unCroaked this thread with Croakamancer in mind (neither one of us wanted to clutter DrLoveMonkey's thread, and this thread is one of my bookmarks), I did bump it (possibly against forum ettiquet, apologies Lioness) with a post about the possibility of the Empress's longevity being the result of having a Gemstone of Immortality.<br /> <br /> Which is something I'm interested in discussing further if anyone else is interested.</div> </div> </div> </div>No harm done. I was more concerned about the initial comments about Croakamancer's username but we're past that now.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T09:22:53-08:00","id":1358631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358598#post1358598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, it\u2019s possible, but to me, it\u2019s the least interesting option.<br /> <br /> Consider, for instance, the sorts of limits to immortality provided by sorcerous workings. What might she be doing, to sustain her unnatural longevity? Or perhaps there\u2019s a potent god out there granting her extended years; what might she owe him, and is her recent disappearance his attempt to collect a debt? Maybe her advanced age is the result of an unprecedented change in nature to the Dragon-Blooded\u2019s inner fire, and clever players might deduce means for themselves to do the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we know Ragara is stealing the lifeforce of an Anathema. And we know Her Redness feeds Anathema to the Imperial Manse. And we know(?) she carries the Hearthstone to the Manse.<br /> <br /> So it's not implausible that the burning burdeon of the Sword of Creation is feeding her as she's feeding it.<br /> <br /> It's not something that needs to be nailed down in game, but it makes one wonder what her three Hearthstones are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T10:12:51-08:00","id":1358641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janissary87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358420#post1358420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The peach-juice miracle by bureaucracy thing? That just felt ...ehh... like he's the master of 1K Realm Sorcerers /and/ he single handedly solved a bureaucracy problem that a dozen other leading Dynast DB's thought impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got to contextualize this.<br /> <br /> 1E was a time when you basically weren't allowed to take 5 dots in your character traits in White Wolf games. Exalted had a little more slack, but carried that baggage.<br /> <br /> Look at the 3E sidebar. A new beurocrat has Beurocracy 1. An experienced professional has 2 dots. An expert who can play a whole kingdom has 3 dots.<br /> <br /> Banoba and his advisors have 4 dots. They're so good, they make the experts look like novices.<br /> <br /> Bhagwei is built like a PC. He has 5 dots. And 5 dots in the relevant Attributes. A likely a Specailty in &quot;House Ragara&quot; (or &quot;eating peaches&quot;).<br /> <br /> It's not hard for a starting PC to have more dice to throw at a problem than most published NPCs. Bhagwei may be special for an NPC... but only because he's built to PC spec. He's very much built within the rules of the game (unlike, say, Mnemon who is running around with a unique artifact): your PCs will be similarly able to show up experienced elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T10:36:22-08:00","id":1358647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358641#post1358641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got to contextualize this.<br /> <br /> 1E was a time when you basically weren't allowed to take 5 dots in your character traits in White Wolf games. Exalted had a little more slack, but carried that baggage.<br /> <br /> Look at the 3E sidebar. A new beurocrat has Beurocracy 1. An experienced professional has 2 dots. An expert who can play a whole kingdom has 3 dots.<br /> <br /> Banoba and his advisors have 4 dots. They're so good, they make the experts look like novices.<br /> <br /> Bhagwei is built like a PC. He has 5 dots. And 5 dots in the relevant Attributes. A likely a Specailty in &amp;quot;House Ragara&amp;quot; (or &amp;quot;eating peaches&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> It's not hard for a starting PC to have more dice to throw at a problem than most published NPCs. Bhagwei may be special for an NPC... but only because he's built to PC spec. He's very much built within the rules of the game (unlike, say, Mnemon who is running around with a unique artifact): your PCs will be similarly able to show up experienced elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. Still don't agree (=P) but I see the merits of your arguement.<br /> <br /> And I think this incident in isolation is fine; but this + &quot;too kind for the throne&quot; + 'secret house uniting heritage' is a bit gilding the lily.<br /> <br /> But! I still even like the character! Just, far and away from my favorite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T13:23:39-08:00","id":1358686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358641#post1358641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got to contextualize this.<br /> <br /> 1E was a time when you basically weren't allowed to take 5 dots in your character traits in White Wolf games. Exalted had a little more slack, but carried that baggage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I remembered people getting a bit hot and bothered that the author of the Shadow Lords Revised tribebook had given the sample characters very optimal Attribute + Ability totals in a number of areas, but that book still went to press. Exalted was also a mechanical derivative of the Aeonverse games, and the most recent offerings of it at the time of Exalted 1e not only permitted stats of 5, they encouraged it, because it was supposed to be a part of a character's concept. Aberrant and Adventure even had a two-phase system where transformation points made it super easy to get those maxed-out stats; in the case of Aberrant, it was also super-easy to max out all your human-scale Attributes and get a bunch of Abilities a5 5 dots, with some specialties added on. Even Trinity got in on it with the unpublished manuscript of Asia Ascendant, which gave us the Superior - up to 6 in a category of Attributes and their related Abilities!<br /> <br /> So while stat-shaming for optimal characters may have been the state for the WoD, Exalted had always been a bit of a different animal in this arena.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T15:48:31-08:00","id":1358719,"title":"","content":"I think having an immortality Hearthstone keeping Mnemon young is an interesting and playable circumstance. The players can alter it (storm the Manse!), it has harmony between the narrative and mechanics, and even the art! (Mnemon is pictured building a Manse with demonic laborers in 2e Core). <br /> <br /> I typically depict the Realm-born as east Asian in appearance. Yes, especially with found eggs, a variety of skin-tones and hair colors are observed, but I play them as exceptions rather than the rule. I particularly like some bit of lore (perhaps from Compass: Wyld) that says the nearest Elemental Pole begins to change the appearance of the mortal population, like some kind of hyper-Demesne. So that you get blue hair in the West after a few generations <i>even if you're on a remote island and your society doesn't intermarry with any blue-haired Westerners!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T16:08:39-08:00","id":1358723,"title":"","content":"The Realm is literally the centre of the world, and has been the capital of world-spanning empires for thousands of years. Yes, when the Primordials made humans the ones on the Blessed Isle looked kind of Chinese (in 3rd ed), but since then there's been so much movement that all kinds of ethnic groups (and mixes thereof) are common and not generally considered important (aside from standards of beauty).<br /> Of course, it could be that due to the presence of the Imperial Mountain people are more likely to have white hair or something, but I think it's not a big thing.<br /> Still, it's a fun thing to play up if you want Creation's humans to look more exotic.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that there isn't xenophobic bigotry in the Realm, but it's unlikely to be very colour-based (which is somewhat historically unusual) at this point. It's accent (a good Realm accent or a stupid barbarian accent), clothes (the veils of a Delzahn man? They look like letterboxes!), place of birth (perhaps, like the Romans, they believe character is influenced by your environment, and so those born and raised close to the Pole of Earth are deemed more rational than the hot-tempered southerners or decadent easterners), and most of all, religious practices.<br /> If you're an Arjuf native who looks kind of An-Tengian, you might have people wondering if you are a foreigner. But if you have a Realm name, wear Realm clothes, eat Realm food, etc, you're fine.<br /> If, on the other hand, you have an An-Tengian name, speak with a bit of an An-Tengian accent, and don't go to shrines much, people might accuse you of being a secret worshipper of the Golden Lord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-03-2020, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T16:22:12-08:00","id":1358728,"title":"","content":"It's kind of an interesting topic for me. Because Creation's kind of well-not-exactly-struggling-with but there's this thing where people in regions are kind of looking like what seemed best to evoke a kind of fantasy trope I guess (so Realm folk are tall with light skin and strong noses, per 1e core, etc). But actually we know from the kind of transformations that we know happened through history in our world, that the First Age, simply by the kind of sweep of transport technologies and economies and empires, probably would have seen huge amounts of movement to the point it's kind of hard to see how that could happen (that you have distinctively different appearance by region)... So I kind of actually don't know how to treat it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T03:06:53-08:00","id":1358808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358723#post1358723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, when the Primordials made humans the ones on the Blessed Isle looked kind of Chinese (in 3rd ed)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wan were the most common ethnic group after the Great Contagion. Unless I've missed something big there's no indication they've been there since before the Primordial War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T03:16:40-08:00","id":1358810,"title":"","content":"I think, even in the First Age, there probably wasn't so much movement as to completely destroy ethnic markers; it's a big world, and while Exalts could fly around on magic sky chariots, your average farmer was using a donkey or her own two feet.<br /> Places on major trade routes would likely be way more mixed than the distant periphery, as places like the Neck or deep desert would have less visitors.<br /> <br /> <br /> However, thinking about the point you raise; people moving thousands of years ago is not actually going to lead to modern diversity per-se, because they'll have interbred with the natives. If an area of easterners had a steady stream of southern labourers and merchants in the First Age, it's unlikely you'll find a large community of black-skinned people there; rather, the locals will sometimes have darker skin or curly hair. Like how Saudi Arabia is opposite Ethiopia and South Sudan, and so Saudis vary between having brown skin or being as pale as Levantines, but hardly any actually look completely sub-Saharan.<br /> It's only places like Nexus or Arjuf or the Imperial City which have had many travellers in the Second Age where you get a community of people very obviously descended from those across the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T03:24:28-08:00","id":1358813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358808#post1358808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wan were the most common ethnic group after the Great Contagion. Unless I've missed something big there's no indication they've been there since before the Primordial War.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but if they're the biggest ethnic group on the Isle my point is that the most likely reason is they were the ones there at the beginning of the First Age. (Though your modern Wan is probably 20% other ancestry without really realising)<br /> They could have migrated there of course, from say the River Lands, though it'd be more likely that people called Wan intermarried with locals to create a new group that ended up also being called Wan, as with the Anglo-Saxons. <br /> <br /> Though saying this, were there actually mortals on the isle originally, or just the gods?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T03:50:37-08:00","id":1358816,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5319-wizard\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5319\" data-vbnamecard=\"5319\">Wizard</a>, re modern style diversity yeah you would be more likely to have people of homogenised appearance between and within regions, though depending a bit on whether assortative partnering and reproduction maintains structure (castes etc), and the underling &quot;genetic&quot; architecture may also be more &quot;friendly&quot; to this maintainance of structure for Creation humans than RW humans.<br /> <br /> Re little movement in First Age, I guess if you go very much with a version of the First Age where individuals mostly live and reproduce in bucolic, closed communities which are a lot like the Second Age or for most of our history, but with much better health and the like, you can kiiind of sustain that.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I would tend to think that, y'know even fairly low levels like 1% migration per year over 100 years is 100% replacement (0.1% a thousand years) and Creation is going to have tons of mass movements technologies available, and huge patchwork political entities that rise and falls more or less want mobility within their borders for the interests of the rulers, and people will want to move to change their lives (or be forced to by wars, disasters etc). So I don't think even the &quot;Most First Age was idealised ancient village life&quot; would get to much structure being left. I don't think you'd get anything that faintly resembles the kind of ethnic structure in world, which kind of exists as a function of how bad and expensive our mass movement technology was until recently and how limited wide political orders were.<br /> <br /> <br /> Set against this though I guess you have extra magical forces that can maintain and create structure (some Exalted hero of the ancient First Age equivalent of icewalkers or whatever that admits no outsiders, even in small numbers etc), though thinking about that can go to some dark places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T03:54:48-08:00","id":1358817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358813#post1358813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though saying this, were there actually mortals on the isle originally, or just the gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the picture of pre-history that we've had since Ruins of Rathess, is that humans were initially created to serve the Dragon Kings and there's only four breeds because in those days the Blessed Isle was the domain of the gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T05:06:29-08:00","id":1358838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/235466-ragara-bhagwei-is-the-best-character-in-this-goddamned-game?p=1358719#post1358719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I particularly like some bit of lore (perhaps from Compass: Wyld) that says the nearest Elemental Pole begins to change the appearance of the mortal population, like some kind of hyper-Demesne. So that you get blue hair in the West after a few generations <i>even if you're on a remote island and your society doesn't intermarry with any blue-haired Westerners!</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of cool when it comes to features that are different to real world ethnic features and reflect high magic. Blue hair, green skin, etc. Or physical subtle qualities like people from one region having more body heat, colder to the touch, etc.<br /> <br /> I would tend to be averse to it for real world ethnic features because of potential for unfortunate implications and people probably psychologically averse to the idea of the world potentially &quot;washing&quot; away from descendents RW ethnic characteristics they've chosen for their character (often to match the players RW identity or interest in a culture).<br /> <br /> (On a tangent, for an example of magic which affects this sort of thing, in what I think is a misstep in a generally interesting &quot;First Age&quot; equivalent in Godbound, and of the schools of ancient magic clearly modelled on Confucian thought, and I gather from the game's reddit, if taken to extremes, transforms people into effectively mindlessly obedient followers of Confucian doctrine and &quot;proper social relationships&quot;, utterly loyal to the Emperor. OK I guess, maybe, not sure I'd go there but hey. But this also seems to transform anyone not of East Asian appearance to East Asian appearance and to lose memory of who they were before... Unfortunate implications ahoy?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T05:24:07-08:00","id":1358844,"title":"","content":"My headcanon regarding ethnicity in Creation is that humans of the Time of Glory resembled a mixture of early forms of man and stock fantasy humanoids. Essentially thousands of years of interbreeding in modern Creation is already reflected by the fact that humans are no longer stratified by their utility to their old masters (save for the places where the Solars had basically started doing it again).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 01-04-2020, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T05:34:27-08:00","id":1358846,"title":"","content":"Perhaps then, the Wan are originally from the Western Scavenger Lands (whose people look a bit similar) and migrated there.<br /> <br /> Or, much more likely, it may be that the Wan are actually a conglomerate of migrants through the First Age, Shogunate, and post-Contagion migrations. Primarily from the close and densely-populated western Scavenger Lands, but with plenty from other places. But due to all that intermarriage, they appear somewhat homogeneous compared to the arrivals of the last century or so, and so peasants who have great-great-great-great-grandparents from Cherak and Chiaroscuro and Thorns and An-Teng and Paragon and Jiara... consider themselves Wan, the natives of the Isle, and are proud that their ancestors tilled this soil since the beginning of time.<br /> <br /> Ghosthead, there's some interesting stuff there, but I will have to respond when I am not on my phone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}